  "scope": "Recycle only private staged outcomes and explicitly discarded reset/cut-stop/shrink suffixes. Four reducers reuse coefficient vectors; boxes/tadpoles also reuse computed masks. No arithmetic, providers, public representations or dependency pins change.",
  "memory_lifecycle": "A live caller outcome is never borrowed for reuse before publication. Prior staging is recycled before new residue assembly, after structural validation. All fallible callbacks finish before new buffers are taken. Publishing still swaps complete outcome slices. Reset and skipped stages explicitly discard their old outcomes into private pools.",
  "retention_bound": "Per reducer, pool plus live/staged banks retain at most two times the largest observed outcome row count of coefficient buffers, and likewise masks where applicable. Allocation happens only when the pool is empty during final assembly; at that point only one caller bank and at most one new bank exist. Reset, cut-stop and numerical failures only move existing buffers. No public storage introspection added.",
